   "subject": "How to include Quadratic latent varible in a model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The following is my SEM model<br>abc = &#39;WLB ~ EXT+OPE+EMO+CON+AGR<br>AGR =~ AGR1+AGR2<br>EXT =~ EXT1+EXT2 (but this variable has quadratic relationship, rather than linear)<br>EMO =~ EMO1+EMO2<br>CON =~ CON1+CON2<br>AGE =~ AGR1+AGR2<br>WLB =~ WLB1+WLB2+WLB3+WLB&#39;<br><br>I just want to know is it possible to include the quadratic effect in the model rather than the liner effect for the latent variable EXT.<br><br>Thank you<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hg6bucz8AwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-05-13T11:06:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to include Quadratic latent varible in a model",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I just want to know is it possible to include the quadratic effect in the model rather than the liner effect for the latent variable EXT.<br></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>In lavaan, only using product indicators (see References in the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ?indProd </font>help page of the semTools package).  For latent moderated structures (LMS, à la M<i>plus</i>), you can patiently) estimate latent quadratic and interaction effects in the nlsem package.</div><div><br></div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div>UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425569662000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0scSMw2yNSR5hJPkkCiCKC\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
